in 1885. On the same day, in the same competition and just 18 miles away, D=
undee Harp defeated Aberdeen Rovers 35-0. Arbroath and Harp were rivals and=
 after the final whistle, officials from Harp sent a telegram to Arbroath s=
imply containing the result of their match and then retired to a pub to cel=
ebrate their world record. Later that evening, a reply was received which r=
ead =E2=80=98Arbroath 36-0 Bon Accord=E2=80=99. Both sides thought the othe=
r was winding them up. The results were not a surprise. Rovers and Bon Acco=
